Here’s a more polished, GitHub-ready README version with proper Markdown, headings, and formatting:

AI Consulting Landing Page – React
A single-page, responsive landing site for an AI Consulting Business built with React.
It includes a hero section, services, a “How we work” process, and a working contact form wired to EmailJS.

✨ Features
Modern hero section with value-focused copy and dual CTAs (“Book a strategy call”, “View services”).

Services section with cards for AI strategy, LLM prototyping, automation, and team enablement.

How we work section with a 4‑step process and interactive 3D tilt hover effect on each step card.

Responsive layout using CSS Grid and Flexbox, optimized for mobile first.

Sticky, glassmorphism-style navbar with logo, anchor links, and a CTA button.

Professional footer with brand block, quick links, contact info, and “Book call” CTA.

Functional contact form:

Name, email, company, budget, and project description fields

Integrated with EmailJS for email delivery

Loading state, success and error messages

🧱 Tech Stack
Frontend: React (Vite or Create React App)

Styling: Custom CSS (mobile-first, dark theme, gradients, 3D hover effects)

Email: EmailJS (client-side email sending from contact form)

🚀 Getting Started
1. Clone and install
bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/ai-consulting-landing.git
cd ai-consulting-landing
npm install
2. Environment variables (EmailJS)
Create a .env file in the project root and add your EmailJS credentials.

For Vite:

bash
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key
For Create React App:

bash
REACT_APP_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id
REACT_APP_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id
REACT_APP_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key
Make sure your EmailJS template variables match the form field names:

user_name

user_email

user_company

user_budget

message

3. Run in development
bash
# Vite
npm run dev

# or CRA
npm start
Open the URL from the terminal (e.g. http://localhost:5173 for Vite).

📁 Project Structure
text
src/
  components/
    Hero.jsx        // Hero section with main headline and CTAs
    Services.jsx    // Service cards for different AI offerings
    Process.jsx     // "How we work" steps with tilt hover effect
    Contact.jsx     // Contact form integrated with EmailJS
    Footer.jsx      // Footer with brand, links, and CTA
    Tilt.jsx        // Reusable mouse-based 3D tilt wrapper
  App.jsx           // Main layout and section composition
  index.css         // Global styles, layout, responsive rules
  main.jsx / index.js
🧩 Key Components
Hero
Strong headline and subheadline focused on business outcomes.

Primary CTA scrolls to the contact section.

Secondary CTA scrolls to the services section.

Small stat cards for social proof / impact metrics.

Services
Config-driven array of services.

Renders cards with title and short description for each AI offering.

How We Work (Process)
4 steps: Discovery, Opportunity mapping, Prototype & iterate, Scale & handover.

Each step wrapped in a Tilt component for a 3D tilt effect that follows cursor movement.

Contact Form
Fields: Name, Work email, Company, Rough budget (select), Message textarea.

Uses emailjs.sendForm with useRef to submit the form.

Displays “Sending…”, success, and error messages.

Footer
Brand logo and tagline.

Quick navigation links (Services, How we work, Contact).

Legal line and placeholders for Privacy / Terms.

Call-to-action button to jump back to the contact form.

🎨 Customization
You can easily tweak:

Branding: Names, logo initials (NA), and colors in App.jsx, Hero.jsx, Footer.jsx, and index.css.

Copy: Text in hero, services, process steps, and contact copy.

Services & steps: Edit the arrays in Services.jsx and Process.jsx.

Theme: Adjust CSS variables in the :root of index.css (accent color, background, etc.).

🌐 Deployment
You can deploy this app to any static hosting platform (Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Pages, etc.).

Example (Vercel):

bash
npm run build
vercel
Make sure your EmailJS environment variables are also set in your hosting provider’s dashboard.

🧠 Ideas for Next Improvements
Add basic spam protection (honeypot field or reCAPTCHA).

Add testimonials and logos of “trusted by” companies.

Add smooth-scroll and active-link highlighting in the navbar.

Track analytics events for CTA clicks and form submissions.

